 ### SCENARIO-PHASE4-073: Exp4317 Either Banks One Adapter-Free Reproduced Level Or Stops Honestly
 **Description:** Running Exp 4317 either writes `blocked_arc_env_unreachable` when the offline ARC environment cannot reset the selected target, writes `blocked_arc_solver_cannot_act` when no adapter-free action can be taken in the selected environment, writes `complete: adapter_free_no_advance_<game>_L<n>_<reason>` only after `exploration_actions_used>0` real actions have been taken without a reproduced level increment, or writes `success: adapter_free_incremental_progress_<game>_advanced_to_L<n>_total23` only when the offline real environment confirms at least one new level and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` independently reproduces the claimed level. A successful run MUST set `total_levels=23`, `levels_completed=1`, `game_advanced` to the selected non-`r11l`/`ls20`/`wa30`/`sc25` game id, `real_env_confirmed=true`, `offline_reproduced=true`, `exploration_actions_used>0`, `submitted_to_leaderboard=false`, preserve the `recommend_approach()` routing evidence, preserve graph-explore trajectory evidence, and compute `reproducibility_checksum` from deterministic solver inputs, preconditions, trajectory, real environment outcome, and reproduction gate result. A decision-grade no-advance run MUST keep `total_levels=22`, set `levels_completed=0`, keep `game_advanced` equal to the selected target game for attribution, set `real_env_confirmed=false`, set `offline_reproduced=false`, set `exploration_actions_used>0`, and satisfy the acceptance gate only because the verdict is terminal-prefixed with `complete:`. A blocked run MUST keep `total_levels=22`, set `levels_completed=0`, set `game_advanced="none"`, record the failed precondition, avoid leaderboard submission, and satisfy the acceptance gate only when the verdict is `blocked_arc_env_unreachable` or `blocked_arc_solver_cannot_act`.
+
+### REQ-PHASE4-074: ARC-AGI-3 E3 Executable World Model Exp4327 ar25 Offline Attempt
+**Description:** The system SHALL run Exp 4327 as an offline, no-leaderboard E3 executable-world-model attempt on `ar25`. It MUST first confirm that `environment_files/ar25/` is non-empty, that `python/carnot/agentic/arc_executable_world_model.py` imports, and that the task performs no TRM training and does not modify `scripts/research_conductor.py`; if the offline ar25 environment is missing it MUST write `honest_verdict="blocked_offline_env_missing_ar25"` and stop. The workflow MUST use the existing `results/arc_e3/ar25/world_model.py` as the induced model deliverable, score verifier reproduction accuracy over offline `collect_transitions("ar25")` data, print and persist `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, execute any induced-model plan only through the real offline environment, and accept an E3 solve only when `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` reports at least one reproduced level. If the bounded round budget ends without such a reproduced solve, it MUST still write an honest partial artifact with the best verifier accuracy and a residual missing-world-model-rule gap. The terminal artifact `results/experiment_4327_e3_executable_world_model_ar25.json` MUST include `honest_verdict`, `verifier_accuracy_per_round`, `world_model_path`, `world_model_sha256`, `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `plan_executed`, `verifier_is_oracle`, `preconditions_checked`, `random_seed`, and `reproducibility_checksum`, with `offline_reproduced`, `reproduced_levels`, `plan_executed`, and `verifier_is_oracle` emitted as bare values rather than principle-wrapped dictionaries. The artifact field principles SHALL be exactly: `honest_verdict` = `Terminal-prefixed (success_e3_ar25_L1_reproduced or complete_e3_ar25_partial_model_<acc>). A reproduced L1 solve and an honest partial (induced model + residual gap) are BOTH progress per the operator E3 spec.`; `verifier_accuracy_per_round` = `list[float]: the verifier is the moat; its reproduction rate per refactor round is the only trustworthy progress signal for the induced model (validated 61% on ar25).`; `world_model_path` = `results/arc_e3/ar25/world_model.py -- the induced model IS the deliverable.`; `world_model_sha256` = `Hash of the induced world model -- makes the solve auditable/reproducible.`; `offline_reproduced` = `BARE bool: the real env reaches L1 via the induced-model plan, re-gated by arc_solver_kit.reproduce() -- only reproduced levels count (ARC Solve Reproducibility).`; `reproduced_levels` = `BARE int: levels offline-reproduced on ar25 -- the +1 incremental-progress unit (target >=1).`; `plan_executed` = `BARE bool + divergence_step: execution-grounded confirmation; halt-on-divergence prevents trusting a wrong model.`; `verifier_is_oracle` = `BARE bool=true -- the SOLVE is EXECUTION-GROUNDED (the real env defines the win), so an E3 solve is ARC NORTH-STAR PROGRESS, NOT an oracle-distinct verifier-moat headline (the moat is the separate Phase A track).`; `preconditions_checked` = `Records the offline-env presence + harness import + TRM-stand-down; pre-empts the silent-missing-resource fabrication mode.`; `random_seed` = `Determinism precondition for the induction + planning.`; `reproducibility_checksum` = `Hash of the world model + the plan + the reproduce() result; lets a third party re-run.`
+
+### SCENARIO-PHASE4-074: Exp4327 Either Reproduces ar25 L1 Or Records An Honest E3 Partial
+**Description:** Running Exp 4327 either writes `blocked_offline_env_missing_ar25` when the local ar25 simulator is absent, writes `success_e3_ar25_L1_reproduced` only when an induced-model plan is executed without trusting a divergent model and `arc_solver_kit.reproduce()` independently reaches at least L1 offline, or writes `complete_e3_ar25_partial_model_<acc>` when the bounded model-refinement/planning attempt does not reach the reproduced-L1 gate. A successful run MUST set `offline_reproduced=true`, `reproduced_levels>=1`, `plan_executed=true`, `verifier_is_oracle=true`, and compute the reproducibility checksum from the world-model hash, plan, and reproduction result. A partial run MUST set `offline_reproduced=false`, `reproduced_levels=0`, preserve the world-model path and hash, persist the best verifier accuracy, and record the residual mismatch class as a missing-world-model-rule gap.
